    "created_at": "2015-11-23T18:48:37Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-11-23T18:48:44Z",
    "body": "We don't want scroll to `(0,0)`. \n\nManual scroll restoration mode means that the browser refrains from setting the scroll position during the navigation. This allows the user script can adjust scroll position if necessary without interference from browser.\n\nNote that this only result in scroll position `(0,0)` when page is loaded from network (i.e., `pageshow.persisted==false`), but it may result in last known scroll position when page is loaded from bfcache  (i.e., `pageshow.persisted==true`) or during some same document navigations (e.g., when the document viewport or size is not modified).\n\nI think your interpretation that in this case \"no scroll restoration is happening\" is valid so perhaps we do not need to modify the wording in the spec to call this case out. Maybe a note to describe the above is helpful?\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
