    "created_at": "2015-11-23T19:03:59Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-11-23T19:03:59Z",
    "body": "I'm worried that given that some browsers don't support bfcache, so .persisted is always false, they effectively scroll to 0,0 because they always load the page from network or local (non-bf-)cache.\nAnd some pages which then start to use 'manual', expect that 'manual' means 0,0 when doing\ncross-page navigations, but those pages would be then broken in browsers which support bfcache.\n\nI don't have any good proposal to improve this in the current API.\n(if we had some event which one needs to cancel to prevent scrolling, the event could contain more information about history navigation and possible scrolling. But event based approach had some other issues)\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
