    "created_at": "2015-11-23T19:55:12Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-11-23T19:55:12Z",
    "body": "I think we should simply say that when restoring a preserved page into view, the scroll position of the page, and anything in it, is left as-is.\n\nGenerally speaking, going back to a bfcached always results in different behavior since the state of the DOM, and the JS object graph of the page, is restored.\n\nWe shouldn't think of bfcache as being equivalent to reloading the page from the network. We should think of bfcache as being equivalent to having opened the next page in a separate tab and then closing that tab. Clearly that scenario wouldn't change the scroll position of anything in the page.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/159045200/reactions",
