    "created_at": "2015-11-25T22:12:35Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-11-25T22:12:35Z",
    "body": "I'm worried that we add a bad API which doesn't make sense in case there is bfcache.\n'load' handling explicitly makes bfcache possible, and pageshow makes it possible to tweak handling if really needed. But here we're adding a flag which behaves very differently whether your UA supports bfcache \nYou press back button and either the previous page (which had 'manual' set) is scrolled to 0,0 or\nit is not - all depending on whether UA supports bfcache.\nCurrently bfcache by default just works, but the change here makes bfcache and non-bfcache cases behave very differently.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
