    "created_at": "2015-11-25T23:21:58Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-11-25T23:21:58Z",
    "body": "I don't think the inconsistency is going to cause any issues given the situation with same-doc navigation and the existence of a simple guarantee in the form on `window.scrollTo(0,0)`. I will make sure MDN documentation is updated to make this clear as well.\n\nAs for the spec, how about adding the following note to \"7.6.10.1 Persisted user state restoration\":\n\n> Not restoring the scroll position by user agent (i.e., `scrollRestoration: manual`) does not mean that the scroll position will be set to any particular value (e.g., `(0,0)`). The actual scroll position depends the type of navigation and user agent's particular caching strategy. So web applications should not expect a particular scroll position but rather should set it to what they want.\"\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
